---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Hexagonal Wire Mesh (Chicken Wire) — Specs, Prices & Anping Factories" description="Hexagonal wire mesh for poultry, gabions, and fencing. Galvanized & PVC coated specs, opening sizes, and direct factory sourcing from Anping, China.">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 flex flex-col lg:flex-row gap-8">
    <!-- Main Content -->
    <article class="flex-1 min-w-0 prose">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-theme-primary">Hexagonal Wire Mesh</h1>
      <p class="text-theme-secondary">Hexagonal wire mesh — also called chicken wire, poultry netting, or hex mesh — is woven from galvanized or PVC-coated wire in a hexagonal pattern. Anping factories produce it for poultry fencing, rockfall protection, gabion boxes, and garden applications.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Materials & Coatings</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Wire</th><th>Coating</th><th>Lifespan</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Electro galvanized</td><td>0.5–1.2mm</td><td>7–15 g/m² zinc</td><td>1–3 years</td><td>Indoor / short-term</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hot-dip galvanized</td><td>0.5–2.0mm</td><td>40–60 g/m² zinc</td><td>5–10 years</td><td>Outdoor fencing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PVC coated</td><td>0.8–2.0mm core</td><td>Plastic over galvanized</td><td>8–15 years</td><td>Decorative / coastal</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Galfan (Zn-Al)</td><td>0.5–2.0mm</td><td>95% Zn + 5% Al</td><td>15–25 years</td><td>Gabions / marine</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Common specifications</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Opening (mm)</th><th>Wire (mm)</th><th>Width (m)</th><th>Length (m)</th><th>Application</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>13</td><td>0.7–0.9</td><td>0.5–2.0</td><td>10–50</td><td>Poultry / small animal</td></tr>
          <tr><td>20</td><td>0.7–1.0</td><td>0.5–2.0</td><td>10–50</td><td>Rabbit / garden</td></tr>
          <tr><td>25</td><td>0.8–1.2</td><td>0.5–2.0</td><td>10–50</td><td>Chicken / light fence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>40</td><td>1.0–1.6</td><td>0.5–2.0</td><td>10–50</td><td>Gabion / rockfall</td></tr>
          <tr><td>50</td><td>1.2–2.0</td><td>0.5–2.0</td><td>10–50</td><td>Heavy gabion / erosion</td></tr>
          <tr><td>75</td><td>1.6–2.5</td><td>0.5–2.0</td><td>10–30</td><td>Large gabion / riverbank</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Hex mesh is sold by roll weight or square meters. <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">Estimate weight →</a></p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">What to specify when ordering</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Opening size in mm (mesh count is NOT used for hexagonal wire)</li>
        <li>Wire diameter and coating type (electro vs hot-dip vs PVC)</li>
        <li>Roll width and length</li>
        <li>Total quantity in m² or rolls</li>
        <li>For gabions: whether mesh needs to be woven or welded, and cell size</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Price reference</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Product</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Spec</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Price Range (USD/roll)</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">MOQ</th>
              <th class="text-left p-3 border border-theme bg-theme-tertiary font-semibold text-theme-primary">Lead Time</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Electro galvanized hex</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">25mm opening, 0.8mm wire, 1×50m</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$8–15/roll</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100 rolls</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">10–15 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Hot-dip galvanized hex</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">25mm opening, 1.0mm wire, 1×50m</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$15–28/roll</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100 rolls</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">12–18 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">PVC coated hex (green)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">25mm opening, 1.0mm core, 1×50m</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$22–38/roll</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">100 rolls</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–20 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Galfan gabion hex</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50–75mm opening, 2.0mm wire</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$18–35/roll</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 rolls</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">15–25 days</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-theme">
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">Heavy hex for rockfall</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">40mm opening, 1.6mm wire, Galfan</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">$25–45/roll</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">50 rolls</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-theme text-theme-secondary">18–28 days</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-theme-muted mb-6">*Indicative 2025–2026 ranges. Actual pricing depends on zinc coating weight, wire cost, order volume, and packaging. Always request formal quotes.</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">FAQ</h2>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What's the difference between hexagonal wire mesh and welded wire mesh?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Hex mesh is <strong>woven</strong> — wires twist around each other in a hexagonal pattern, giving flexibility and conformability. Welded wire mesh has wires welded at intersections, creating rigid squares or rectangles. Hex is cheaper and better for curved surfaces (gabions, poultry); welded is stronger and better for flat panels.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How long does galvanized hex mesh last outdoors?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Electro galvanized (7–15 g/m² zinc): 1–3 years. Hot-dip galvanized (40–60 g/m²): 5–10 years. Galfan (Zn-Al alloy): 15–25 years even in marine environments. PVC coating adds cosmetic protection but the wire underneath still determines structural life.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Can I use hex mesh for gabion boxes?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes — woven hex mesh is the traditional gabion material. For permanent structures, specify Galfan or heavy hot-dip zinc coating, 2.0mm+ wire, and 50–75mm openings. Welded gabions (like our <a href="/products/gabion-baskets/" class="text-theme-accent">gabion baskets</a>) are newer and more rigid but cost more.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">What mesh opening for chickens vs rabbits?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Chickens: 25mm opening keeps predators out. Rabbits: 20mm or 25mm. Small birds/quail: 13mm. For garden pest control against rabbits, 25mm with 1.0mm+ wire is standard.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">Is PVC coated hex mesh safe for animals?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Yes, if the coating is UV-stabilized and lead-free. Ask for a coating thickness report (usually 0.4–0.6mm PVC over galvanized core). Green and black are standard colors; custom colors need larger MOQs.</p>
      </details>
      
      <details class="mb-3 border border-theme rounded-lg bg-theme-card">
        <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer p-4 text-theme-primary hover:text-theme-accent transition">How do I calculate how many rolls I need?</summary>
        <p class="text-sm mt-2 px-4 pb-4 text-theme-secondary">Measure fence length × height = m² needed. Divide by roll coverage (width × length). Add 5–10% for overlaps and cuts. Use our <a href="/tools/container-loading-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent">container loading calculator</a> to plan shipment.</p>
      </details>

      <div class="not-prose mt-8 bg-theme-secondary text-white rounded-xl p-6">
        <p class="font-semibold text-lg">Get quotes from Anping hex mesh factories</p>
        <a href="/inquiry/" class="inline-block mt-3 accent-bg hover:accent-bg font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Send an inquiry →</a>
      </div>
    </article>

